<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arthur Phillip</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1738–1814</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arthur Phillip was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a> officer who commanded the First Fleet of convict ships to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>. He founded the settlement at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sydney-cove">Sydney Cove</a> in January 1788 and served as the first governor of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-wales">South Wales</a> until 1792, guiding the colony through its early food shortages.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arthur-phillip.jpg" alt="Arthur Phillip" width="320" height="376" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francis Wheatley · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arthur_Phillip_-_Wheatley_ML124_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
